#X obj 659 11 env.follow~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 341 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 An envelope follower: tracks the amplitude of the incoming
audio signal and outputs a smooth control signal representing its current
level. The follower uses independent attack and release times \, so
rising and falling portions of the signal can be smoothed at different
rates.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Envelope-controlled effects — driving the amount
of distortion \, filter cutoff \, or modulation depth from the current
level of the input signal \, so that the effect reacts to the music.;
#X text 250 279 • Side-chain compression and gating — using the follower
output as a control signal for a compressor or gate \, so that another
signal is reduced or opened based on the level of the source.;
#X text 250 349 • Automatic gain control — keeping the output level
of a signal roughly constant by adjusting gain according to the follower
output.;
